.TH CLRUCACHE_SIZE 3 "2026-08-02" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
clrucache_size \- return the number of live entries in the cache
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/clrucache.h>

size_t clrucache_size(clru_cache cache);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns the number of live entries in the cache at the moment. A live
entry is one that is fully initialised and that no eviction has
removed, so a placeholder entry created by a fetch or a set in
progress is not counted.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cache  Cache handle.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
The number of live entries. It is 0 when cache is CLRU_CACHE_INVALID,
and 0 when cache is a stale handle that a call already destroyed.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
cache is an opaque VALUE handle, which the library resolves through a
slot table of its own before it touches the cache object behind it. A
stale handle is an ordinary error here and not a fatal one; only
clru_destroy() treats a stale handle as fatal.
The function adds up the sizes of the cache's segments, taking each
segment's own lock in turn. So the result is a snapshot and not a
value at one instant: a segment can gain or lose an entry after it has
been counted, and the total describes no single moment.
The complexity is O(number of segments), a small fixed bound, not
O(entries).
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR clrucache_capacity (3),
.BR clrucache_create_full (3)
